      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-15T23:50:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It does seem a bit odd to me</p><p>that that is the way it would be</p><p>but the text has no \"if\"</p><p>that would cause it to whiff</p><p>So it might be behaving correctly</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The Operative explicitly only deals damage if she's not incapped. &nbsp;Since the Chairman doesn't have the \"if active\" clause, it would imply that he can still deal damage.</p><p>The counter argument there is that the Operative needs the \"if\" clause because she doesn't leave play when she's incapped, while the Chairman does. &nbsp;Since he's not in play, he shouldn't be able to deal damage.</p>",
